1
00:00:06,981 --> 00:00:08,681
You are seeing these words.

2
00:00:08,761 --> 00:00:10,596
Somewhere a sound is going on.

3
00:00:10,676 --> 00:00:14,210
Your body is resting on
something. A thought passes.

4
00:00:14,290 --> 00:00:20,290
Six streams, all at once, and all of it
feels like one life, lived by one someone.

5
00:00:21,374 --> 00:00:25,832
Here is the question. If no self is
carried from this moment to the next,

6
00:00:25,912 --> 00:00:27,531
is everything cut off?

7
00:00:27,611 --> 00:00:29,940
And at death, do I simply end?

8
00:00:30,749 --> 00:00:35,863
This is After Anatta: notes by
John Tan, known as Thusness.

9
00:00:36,694 --> 00:00:42,022
The fear of being cut off sounds like the
opposite of clinging to a self. It is not.

10
00:00:42,102 --> 00:00:47,199
It clings to the same self, and only
changes the story of what happens to it.

11
00:00:47,279 --> 00:00:51,252
Something can be cut off only if it
was there from its own side first.

12
00:00:51,382 --> 00:00:53,122
"It ends" still needs an "it".

13
00:00:53,202 --> 00:00:58,204
So the hope of being carried over and
the fear of being cut off share one root.

14
00:00:58,284 --> 00:01:04,024
A thing with a being of its own, which
either goes on for ever, or is destroyed.

15
00:01:04,837 --> 00:01:07,909
Nāgārjuna answers both with one reason.

16
00:01:07,989 --> 00:01:12,433
Whatever comes to be in dependence
on something is not that very thing,

17
00:01:12,513 --> 00:01:14,431
and it is not other than it either.

18
00:01:14,511 --> 00:01:17,030
So it is neither cut off nor permanent.

19
00:01:17,849 --> 00:01:21,138
Most explanations reach
for outside images here.

20
00:01:21,218 --> 00:01:22,945
A seed and its plant.

21
00:01:23,025 --> 00:01:24,820
One flame lighting another.

22
00:01:24,900 --> 00:01:27,483
They help, but they are
watched from outside.

23
00:01:27,563 --> 00:01:31,356
Let us start somewhere closer,
where this can be felt directly.

24
00:01:31,436 --> 00:01:35,205
In your own seeing, hearing
and thinking, right now.

25
00:01:36,034 --> 00:01:41,715
There is seeing. These letters, the light,
the colours around them. There is hearing.

26
00:01:41,795 --> 00:01:45,234
A fan, a car, a voice in another room.

27
00:01:45,314 --> 00:01:50,166
There is smelling and tasting, faint
perhaps, but there when you notice them.

28
00:01:50,246 --> 00:01:54,270
There is touching. The weight of your
body, the temperature of the air.

29
00:01:54,349 --> 00:01:55,492
And there is thinking.

30
00:01:55,572 --> 00:01:59,369
The words being understood, a
thought about something else.

31
00:02:00,169 --> 00:02:03,581
The Buddha counted these as
six kinds of consciousness.

32
00:02:03,661 --> 00:02:07,059
And he said each one arises
with its own conditions.

33
00:02:07,139 --> 00:02:11,135
Dependent on the eye and forms,
eye-consciousness arises.

34
00:02:11,215 --> 00:02:13,553
Seeing arises with eye and colour.

35
00:02:13,633 --> 00:02:16,411
Hearing arises with ear and sound.

36
00:02:16,500 --> 00:02:19,545
Thinking arises with
mind and what is thought.

37
00:02:19,625 --> 00:02:24,790
Each stream is fully itself. Seeing
does not hear. Hearing does not see.

38
00:02:24,870 --> 00:02:26,669
No smell has ever been heard.

39
00:02:27,485 --> 00:02:31,943
And yet these six do not feel like
six strangers. You see the cup.

40
00:02:32,023 --> 00:02:36,481
You reach for it. You feel its
warmth, smell the tea, taste it.

41
00:02:36,561 --> 00:02:38,981
You hear the small sound
as you set it down,

42
00:02:39,061 --> 00:02:40,924
and think, that's better.

43
00:02:41,004 --> 00:02:42,595
Seeing guides the hand.

44
00:02:42,675 --> 00:02:44,714
Touch confirms what seeing showed.

45
00:02:44,794 --> 00:02:46,902
The thought takes up
what the tongue found.

46
00:02:46,982 --> 00:02:50,842
It all hangs together so smoothly
that it feels like one someone,

47
00:02:50,922 --> 00:02:54,157
who sees and hears and tastes and thinks.

48
00:02:54,237 --> 00:02:57,731
In refined practice it feels
like something subtler still.

49
00:02:57,811 --> 00:03:02,654
A pure awareness, the same in all
six, quietly there behind them.

50
00:03:03,492 --> 00:03:08,643
Here, almost without fail, the
substantialist mind makes one move.

51
00:03:08,723 --> 00:03:12,950
It takes the six streams, each
arising with its conditions,

52
00:03:13,030 --> 00:03:15,912
and pulls out of them
a single consciousness.

53
00:03:15,992 --> 00:03:18,385
One awareness that sees through the eyes,

54
00:03:18,465 --> 00:03:22,624
hears through the ears, and
runs from one sense to the next.

55
00:03:22,704 --> 00:03:27,193
The thread that joins them. The one still
there when seeing gives way to hearing.

56
00:03:28,010 --> 00:03:31,178
The Buddha met this view
in a monk named Sāti.

57
00:03:31,258 --> 00:03:35,009
Sāti held that it is this very
same consciousness that roams and

58
00:03:35,089 --> 00:03:37,591
transmigrates, not another.

59
00:03:37,671 --> 00:03:39,330
He did not posit a soul.

60
00:03:39,410 --> 00:03:44,425
He posited consciousness itself as
the carrier. The Buddha corrected him.

61
00:03:44,505 --> 00:03:47,020
Consciousness is dependently arisen.

62
00:03:47,100 --> 00:03:50,226
Without its conditions,
there is no consciousness.

63
00:03:50,306 --> 00:03:54,968
It is named by what it depends on,
the way a fire is named by its fuel.

64
00:03:55,048 --> 00:03:57,740
A fire burning logs is a log fire.

65
00:03:57,820 --> 00:04:00,607
A fire burning grass is a grass fire.

66
00:04:00,687 --> 00:04:02,604
Seeing is eye-consciousness.

67
00:04:02,684 --> 00:04:04,900
Hearing is ear-consciousness.

68
00:04:04,980 --> 00:04:09,266
There is no consciousness as
such, moving from fuel to fuel.

69
00:04:10,073 --> 00:04:13,213
And notice where the carrier
comes from. Not from looking.

70
00:04:13,293 --> 00:04:16,908
Look, and no carrier is
found. It comes from habit.

71
00:04:16,988 --> 00:04:22,207
The long tendencies of the inherent
framework expect every "and then" to have

72
00:04:22,287 --> 00:04:24,585
a something underneath that goes on.

73
00:04:24,665 --> 00:04:27,656
The six streams work
together so well that,

74
00:04:27,736 --> 00:04:32,343
to this habit, it seems impossible
that nothing holds them together.

75
00:04:32,423 --> 00:04:36,501
So the mind supplies something,
a self or a pure awareness,

76
00:04:36,581 --> 00:04:38,856
without noticing that it supplied it.

77
00:04:39,669 --> 00:04:42,388
Now look at the moment
seeing gives way to hearing.

78
00:04:42,468 --> 00:04:44,833
You are reading, and a sound comes.

79
00:04:44,913 --> 00:04:46,550
Attention turns to it.

80
00:04:47,353 --> 00:04:50,248
Is the hearing the same as the seeing? No.

81
00:04:50,328 --> 00:04:52,001
It has different conditions.

82
00:04:52,081 --> 00:04:54,610
Ear and sound, not eye and colour.

83
00:04:54,690 --> 00:04:57,015
Nothing of the seeing
went into the hearing.

84
00:04:57,095 --> 00:05:01,598
Nothing travelled across. So it is
not the same. Nothing was carried.

85
00:05:02,405 --> 00:05:06,795
Is the hearing cut off from the
seeing, unrelated to it? Also no.

86
00:05:06,875 --> 00:05:09,064
The hearing came in the
middle of the reading.

87
00:05:09,144 --> 00:05:12,094
The thought, what was
that, takes up the sound.

88
00:05:12,174 --> 00:05:15,341
Then you go back to these
lines and find your place.

89
00:05:15,421 --> 00:05:17,420
The streams are woven together.

90
00:05:17,500 --> 00:05:21,659
Each one shapes what the others do
next. So it is not different either.

91
00:05:21,739 --> 00:05:22,939
Nothing was cut.

92
00:05:23,697 --> 00:05:25,560
Neither same nor different.

93
00:05:25,640 --> 00:05:28,861
Neither carried nor cut.
And it is not a theory.

94
00:05:28,941 --> 00:05:31,678
You can watch it happen,
many times a minute.

95
00:05:32,498 --> 00:05:35,081
But first, look at what
is actually happening,

96
00:05:35,161 --> 00:05:37,011
before anything is lined up.

97
00:05:37,091 --> 00:05:39,769
In real time there has
never been a carrier.

98
00:05:39,849 --> 00:05:42,378
Not a hidden one, not a subtle one.

99
00:05:42,458 --> 00:05:44,171
Each instant is complete.

100
00:05:44,251 --> 00:05:46,291
The seeing is wholly seeing.

101
00:05:46,371 --> 00:05:48,057
The sound is wholly sound.

102
00:05:48,137 --> 00:05:49,769
The thought is wholly thought.

103
00:05:49,849 --> 00:05:52,663
Nothing is missing that a
carrier would have to supply.

104
00:05:52,743 --> 00:05:55,262
Nothing in it is waiting to be handed on.

105
00:05:56,081 --> 00:05:58,080
Complete does not mean sealed off.

106
00:05:58,160 --> 00:06:03,854
Each instant arises with its conditions,
and its conditions are woven with others.

107
00:06:03,934 --> 00:06:06,205
It means only that nothing is lacking.

108
00:06:06,285 --> 00:06:08,043
So there is nothing to bridge.

109
00:06:08,866 --> 00:06:12,169
The question, what carries
me from this to the next,

110
00:06:12,249 --> 00:06:14,221
does not come up in the instant.

111
00:06:14,301 --> 00:06:17,129
It comes up only when the mind steps back,

112
00:06:17,209 --> 00:06:20,716
lines the instants up one
after another in time,

113
00:06:20,796 --> 00:06:23,641
and looks at the spaces
it has drawn between them.

114
00:06:24,457 --> 00:06:29,621
And when we do line them up, as we must,
to speak of yesterday and tomorrow,

115
00:06:29,701 --> 00:06:34,417
of growing up and growing old, this
is how the line is rightly described.

116
00:06:34,497 --> 00:06:36,360
Neither same nor different.

117
00:06:36,440 --> 00:06:39,648
Neither carried nor cut.
And here is the key.

118
00:06:39,728 --> 00:06:43,725
That is not a description of a
gap that continuity has to cross.

119
00:06:43,805 --> 00:06:45,301
It is the continuity.

120
00:06:45,381 --> 00:06:49,119
There is nothing more behind it,
holding the streams together.

121
00:06:49,199 --> 00:06:53,018
The weaving of the six streams,
none the same as another,

122
00:06:53,098 --> 00:06:58,090
none cut off from another, is the whole
of what we have always called going on.

123
00:06:58,914 --> 00:07:01,728
The substantialist mind
cannot picture this.

124
00:07:01,808 --> 00:07:06,633
Shown seeing, and then hearing, it
pictures two banks of a river with a gap

125
00:07:06,713 --> 00:07:10,207
between them. And it asks,
what crosses the gap?

126
00:07:10,287 --> 00:07:13,132
It looks for a carrier
to bridge the transition.

127
00:07:13,249 --> 00:07:17,679
Finding none, it concludes,
then I am cut off every moment,

128
00:07:17,759 --> 00:07:19,803
and cut off for good at death.

129
00:07:20,638 --> 00:07:23,330
But the two banks were
never standing on their own.

130
00:07:23,410 --> 00:07:25,422
No gap stands between them.

131
00:07:25,502 --> 00:07:28,819
So no bridge is needed,
and no one has to cross.

132
00:07:28,899 --> 00:07:33,874
Asking what carries me across is like
asking what carries blue across to red,

133
00:07:33,954 --> 00:07:35,794
in a painting where they meet.

134
00:07:36,626 --> 00:07:39,060
The same knot is at work
in holding an apple.

135
00:07:39,140 --> 00:07:43,353
Colour, weight, smell and taste
are each their own appearing.

136
00:07:43,433 --> 00:07:47,769
A habit of the mind ties them
into one solid apple out there.

137
00:07:47,849 --> 00:07:49,671
The self is tied the same way.

138
00:07:49,751 --> 00:07:53,367
Six streams, tied into
one solid someone in here.

139
00:07:53,447 --> 00:07:55,894
And when that coarse self is seen through,

140
00:07:55,974 --> 00:07:58,625
a subtler knot often remains.

141
00:07:58,705 --> 00:08:03,670
A pure, featureless awareness, set
behind the six as their ground.

142
00:08:04,481 --> 00:08:09,618
The answer is not to throw clarity
away. Seeing is clear. Hearing is clear.

143
00:08:09,698 --> 00:08:12,906
Thinking is clear.
Clarity is never missing.

144
00:08:12,986 --> 00:08:15,393
The error is pulling
it out of the streams,

145
00:08:15,473 --> 00:08:18,232
and making it one thing
that stands behind them.

146
00:08:18,312 --> 00:08:21,072
Untie the knot, and nothing is lost.

147
00:08:21,152 --> 00:08:26,090
The six streams go on, as vivid
as before, owned by no one.

148
00:08:26,914 --> 00:08:30,652
Without the time framework,
there is no sequence to describe.

149
00:08:30,732 --> 00:08:32,880
What is here is one complete stroke.

150
00:08:32,960 --> 00:08:36,413
Timeless, total, immediate and complete.

151
00:08:36,493 --> 00:08:41,970
Line it up in time, and the same appearing
is rightly described as neither same nor

152
00:08:42,050 --> 00:08:44,905
different, neither carried nor cut.

153
00:08:44,985 --> 00:08:50,163
These are not two worlds, a timeless
one above and a passing one below.

154
00:08:50,243 --> 00:08:54,909
They are one appearing, seen without
the framework, and seen with it.

155
00:08:55,783 --> 00:08:58,950
Three traditions say
this, each in its own way.

156
00:08:59,030 --> 00:09:03,257
Nāgārjuna says time is not
found apart from what changes.

157
00:09:03,337 --> 00:09:06,844
If not a single thing is
found, how will there be time?

158
00:09:06,924 --> 00:09:10,092
Dzogchen calls itself
the Great Completeness.

159
00:09:10,172 --> 00:09:14,616
Nothing lacking, nothing to add,
and a fourth time beyond past,

160
00:09:14,696 --> 00:09:19,580
present and future. Dōgen says
each moment is the whole of time.

161
00:09:19,696 --> 00:09:24,154
Firewood abides in its own place,
with a before and an after,

162
00:09:24,234 --> 00:09:25,975
yet cut off from both.

163
00:09:26,055 --> 00:09:28,407
Ash does not turn back into firewood.

164
00:09:28,487 --> 00:09:31,523
And still, he says, time passes.

165
00:09:32,333 --> 00:09:33,679
Each needs one guard.

166
00:09:33,759 --> 00:09:37,864
Timeless does not mean a timeless
reality behind appearances.

167
00:09:37,944 --> 00:09:39,467
That would be a new ground.

168
00:09:39,547 --> 00:09:44,535
The completeness of Dzogchen is not a
pure awareness behind the six streams.

169
00:09:44,615 --> 00:09:47,171
It is the six streams themselves.

170
00:09:47,251 --> 00:09:52,076
And Dōgen's "cut off from before and
after" means that nothing carries the

171
00:09:52,156 --> 00:09:56,360
moments. It does not mean that
something is destroyed between them.

172
00:09:57,177 --> 00:09:58,333
So what of sleep?

173
00:09:58,413 --> 00:10:03,143
In deep sleep the streams go quiet,
and no one watches the hours.

174
00:10:03,223 --> 00:10:07,464
It is easy to slip from there to,
so for those hours nothing went on.

175
00:10:07,544 --> 00:10:09,882
That is the cut, sneaking back in.

176
00:10:09,962 --> 00:10:12,939
All night the heart beat
and the breath went on.

177
00:10:13,019 --> 00:10:14,733
Yesterday's learning settled.

178
00:10:14,813 --> 00:10:18,700
In the morning you know your name, and
remember the friend you meant to call.

179
00:10:18,780 --> 00:10:23,306
None of it was carried through the night
by a passenger. None of it was cut off.

180
00:10:23,386 --> 00:10:28,636
Naming does not make continuity, and
the absence of naming does not break it.

181
00:10:29,461 --> 00:10:31,935
And what of death? Nothing is carried.

182
00:10:32,015 --> 00:10:37,546
No soul, no subtle self, no pure
consciousness packs up and moves to a new

183
00:10:37,626 --> 00:10:41,364
body. That was Sāti's
picture. And nothing is cut.

184
00:10:41,444 --> 00:10:43,199
Actions bear their fruit.

185
00:10:43,279 --> 00:10:46,908
The habits of a life give
rise to what comes next,

186
00:10:46,988 --> 00:10:51,392
the way this moment's hearing gives
rise to the thought that follows it.

187
00:10:51,472 --> 00:10:56,718
Rebirth and karma are affirmed, in
the ordinary way the world speaks.

188
00:10:56,798 --> 00:10:59,136
Emptiness does not explain them away.

189
00:10:59,216 --> 00:11:02,646
It only shows that the carrier
and the cut were never found.

190
00:11:03,449 --> 00:11:05,882
So, will I continue after death?

191
00:11:05,962 --> 00:11:08,681
Not, yes, the same I goes on.

192
00:11:08,761 --> 00:11:10,991
Not, no, I simply end.

193
00:11:11,071 --> 00:11:15,040
It is the answer you can already
see between seeing and hearing.

194
00:11:15,120 --> 00:11:17,200
What follows depends on what is now.

195
00:11:17,280 --> 00:11:19,895
It is not the same, and it is not other.

196
00:11:20,722 --> 00:11:23,237
When the teaching says
there is no carrier,

197
00:11:23,317 --> 00:11:27,680
it denies one thing only, a
carrier standing by itself.

198
00:11:27,760 --> 00:11:32,327
It does not add, and therefore
nothing goes on. The habit adds that.

199
00:11:32,407 --> 00:11:34,582
So say both halves, every time.

200
00:11:34,662 --> 00:11:37,780
Nothing is carried over,
and nothing is cut off.

201
00:11:38,593 --> 00:11:40,795
Try it now. Just this instant.

202
00:11:40,875 --> 00:11:43,730
Whatever is seen, heard or felt.

203
00:11:43,810 --> 00:11:47,186
Nothing missing from it,
nothing waiting to be carried.

204
00:11:48,018 --> 00:11:53,359
Then let it go on. Seeing, then a
sound, then a touch, then a thought.

205
00:11:53,439 --> 00:11:55,153
At each change, ask.

206
00:11:55,233 --> 00:11:57,069
Did anything travel across?

207
00:11:57,149 --> 00:11:59,356
Is this one cut off from the last?

208
00:12:00,190 --> 00:12:03,684
Then notice the question that
wants to come. What joins them?

209
00:12:03,764 --> 00:12:06,863
Who goes from one to the
next? Do not answer it.

210
00:12:06,943 --> 00:12:10,599
It is looking for a bridge, and the
streams are going on perfectly well

211
00:12:10,679 --> 00:12:11,879
without one.

212
00:12:12,589 --> 00:12:18,396
Seeing. Hearing. A thought. Each
complete. None carried. None cut.

